was run 'on the 60 individual chamber readings' with n=30 per regime and t(58), i.e., all repeated measurements from the same plot were entered as independent rows into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, whereas only 6 independent plots exist per arm (correct row-independent df would be 10, not 58).\",\"The workflow confirms this: flux_samples() pools every row by water_table_regime with no aggregation by plot_id before calling stats.ttest_ind, so within-plot dependence is ignored and the reported p-value/df are based on pseudoreplicated units.\",\"The minted lock's unit-key authorization lists authorized_key_columns = ['plot_id'], which follows directly from the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: plot_id' in the translation receipt; the extracted token appears in the logical header, and both v1 and v2 lanes minted consistently with that single declared column.\",\"Note the lock authorizes only the declared unit key; it does not certify that the executed procedure respected that unit, and here the procedure did not — the report's headline conclusion rests on 60 rows treated as independent despite the declared 12-plot unit structure.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declaration names plot_id as the independent-unit column; the frozen data contain exactly 12 distinct plots (DR-01..DR-06 in the drained arm, RW-01..RW-06 in the rewetted arm), each appearing exactly 5 times (survey rounds 1-5), matching the data description of 12 plots x 5 visits = 60 rows in both procedure arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states the two-sample Student t-test was run 'on the 60 individual chamber readings' with n=30 per regime and t(58), i.e., all repeated measurements from the same plot were entered as independent rows into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, whereas only 6 independent plots exist per arm (correct row-independent df would be 10, not 58).","The workflow confirms this: flux_samples() pools every row by water_table_regime with no aggregation by plot_id before calling stats.ttest_ind, so within-plot dependence is ignored and the reported p-value/df are based on pseudoreplicated units.","The minted lock's unit-key authorization lists authorized_key_columns = ['plot_id'], which follows directly from the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: plot_id' in the translation receipt; the extracted token appears in the logical header, and both v1 and v2 lanes minted consistently with that single declared column.","Note the lock authorizes only the declared unit key; it does not certify that the executed procedure respected that unit, and here the procedure did not — the report's headline conclusion rests on 60 rows treated as independent despite the declared 12-plot unit structure."]},"ttft_ms":6959,"ttft_stream_ms":1668,"time_to_request_ms":9,"type":"result","duration_ms":14127,"uuid":"5fd30621-96ae-40c5-b4f2-4f18300c9c22"}
